{"reference":"Psalms 24","book":"Psalms","chapter":24,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Interpretive Question","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Psalm 24:1 declares that the earth belongs to Jehovah. A later passage draws on this statement when permitting food sold in the market to be eaten without investigating its provenance. That use treats the psalm’s claim of God’s ownership as relevant to a practical question about ordinary goods.","verse_refs":["Psalms 24:1"],"provenance_refs":["render_path_psalms_024_b233c121aeffdc16fd59f6cb"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}